-- title:
--   The Čech complex of free abelian sheaves of a covering morphism is exact in positive degrees
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category with finite wide pullbacks and $J$ a Grothendieck topology on $\mathcal{C}$ for which presheaves of abelian groups admit sheafification. Let $f : V \to U$ be a morphism such that the sieve generated by $f$ covers $U$. For $n \ge 0$ let
--   $$\mathbb{Z}[V^{(n)}], \qquad V^{(n)} = V \times_U \cdots \times_U V \ \ (n+1 \text{ factors}),$$
--   be the free abelian sheaf on the $n$-th term of the Čech nerve of $f$, and let $d_n : \mathbb{Z}[V^{(n+1)}] \to \mathbb{Z}[V^{(n)}]$ be the Čech differentials. Then for every $n \in \mathbb{N}$ the sequence
--   $$\mathbb{Z}[V^{(n+2)}] \xrightarrow{\ d_{n+1}\ } \mathbb{Z}[V^{(n+1)}] \xrightarrow{\ d_n\ } \mathbb{Z}[V^{(n)}]$$
--   is exact in the category of abelian sheaves.
--
--   Together with exactness at the augmentation, this says that the Čech complex of free sheaves is a resolution of $\mathbb{Z}[U]$ (more precisely, of the free sheaf on the covering sieve, which sheafifies to $\mathbb{Z}[U]$); it is the basis for comparing Čech and derived-functor cohomology.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The site is `C : Type (u+1)` with `[Category.{u} C]` and `[HasFiniteWidePullbacks C]`; sheaves take values in `AddCommGrpCat.{u+1}` and `[HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u+1}]` is assumed. The objects and differentials are `cechFree J f n` and `cechFreeD J f n`, the short complex uses the proof `cechFreeD_comp_d J f n`, and exactness is Mathlib's `ShortComplex.Exact`. The covering hypothesis is `Sieve.generate (Presieve.singleton f) ∈ J U`. The theorem is `CategoryTheory.cechFree_exact_succ`.
-- source:
--   B. Bhatt, P. Scholze, The pro-étale topology for schemes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.1198 (v2, 17 Dec 2014). Lean source: idealson-nexources/proetale (fork of chrisflav/proetale by C. Merten, J. Jiang and contributors, Apache-2.0), commit 2983805, file Proetale/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Sites/SheafCohomology/CechResolution.lean, lines 615-628 (`CategoryTheory.cechFree_exact_succ`).

import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.Grp.Abelian
import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.Grp.Adjunctions
import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.Grp.Colimits
import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.Grp.FilteredColimits
import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.Grp.Limits
import Mathlib.AlgebraicTopology.AlternatingFaceMapComplex
import Mathlib.AlgebraicTopology.ExtraDegeneracy
import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.Abelian
